    "rich_text_8KbrYt": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_qhVPVK": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Your coffee name is called ‘Huddle’ - meaning ‘to crowd together’; what’s your take on creating a space for people to convene, socialise and connect?<br/><br/></strong>Community has always been something important to us. Gathering people around, being a place where people can connect with each other, having a good time and sharing our vision to others has always been the DNA of what Huddle is.<br/><br/><strong>Why are we, and by we I mean us, so addicted to coffee shops? Whether we drink it or not, what do you think makes the space somewhere people can lounge their days away without any judgement?<br/><br/></strong>A coffee shop is a safe place where you can easily escape from the rush of your daily routine. You can meet friends, read a book, or just enjoy the place itself. A coffee shop is a place made for everybody.<br/><br/><strong>You’re not only a Coffee destination, you’re a ‘Creative Space’, what do you think is the future of traditional Coffee shops and do you think the hybrid approach is the way forward?<br/><br/></strong>The “Traditional” coffee shop will always stand. They are such special places that people will always need a coffee shop nearby.<br/>Making a hybrid space is a way for us to be able to talk to our own people - our community. It goes from the music, the space itself, the books, to our customer service. We really wanted to mark the difference between us and the other coffee. We are Huddle and as soon as our vibe is talking to you, you’re Huddle too. This place is much more than a coffee shop, it is a place where creatives, brands or anyone else could be enlightened. We want anyone to feel like they’re at home. Again, it’s all about sharing with our community.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "text_qhVPVK"
      ],
